In article <42467@ut-emx.uucp>, moxley@ccwf.cc.utexas.edu (Richard Moxley) writes:
> I have Mac NetHack 3.0i patch level 9.  How do I get it to play a game in
> Wizard mode?  When I examine the `getname' DITL resource with ResEdit, I
> can see that there is a check box for `debug (WIZARD) mode'.  However,
> when the dialog comes up at the start of the game, this check box is not
> visible.  I tried using a player name of `Wizard' (this was the method used
> for Mac NH 3.0 pl 6), but this didn't work.  Any clues?
> 
> Richard

Well, from my understanding, you must enter 'wizard' as the player name in
the dialog you mentioned. Then you use the SAVE option. Quit the ensuing game
and the next time you start up a game, it should enable that check box. If this
doesn't work, I might not have explained it clearly-- but please download the
info file directly from apple's ftp site (if you can). It's apple.apple.com
in the nethack directory. Do a little checking around if it's not immediately
noticeable.

